# cuts/v1.0.34/cut.env
# ============================================================================
# THE PINS FOR v1.0.34. Read by bin/rollforward_gate.sh --cut v1.0.34 and by
# scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh.
#
# WHY v1.0.34 EXISTS: v1.0.33 IS 33 COMMITS BEHIND AND ANDY HAS NO BOX TO WALK.
#
# v1.0.33 was cut at a1cb850f. Everything merged on 2026-08-17 landed after it,
# including both parser fixes, the enrichment invoker, the enrich budget and
# the wiki page-count oracle. Walking v1.0.33 would rediscover defects that are
# already fixed on main, which is the most expensive thing a box-walk can do.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE TRAP THIS FILE IS THE FOURTH DOCUMENTED VICTIM OF, AND THE FIRST TO BE
# CAUGHT BEFORE THE TAG RATHER THAN AFTER IT
#
# The v1.0.33 record states it in one line: A RE-PIN IS TWO EDITS, NOT ONE.
# Moving the digest in install.sh is the visible half; recording what the digest
# IS, in scripts/wiki_image_provenance.tsv, remains owed, and the gate that
# catches the omission does not run on the PR that commits it.
#
# It happened again. CM051 #809 (520ab31) re-pinned both wiki images to v0.1.18
# and touched install.sh ONLY -- measured, 1 file changed, 2 insertions, 2
# deletions. It added no ledger rows. Its own PR body even wrote the follow-up
# down: "the next cut needs the equivalent rows for 635e3ee7 / c6a207fc against
# bf5dfe68". Nothing enforced it, and all 54 checks on main were green, because
# the provenance gate runs at CUT time and not on the PR.
#
# Measured on main at 25cc231d, before this branch:
#
#     PROV_GATE_ONLY_CLASSES=wiki scripts/provenance_gate.sh   ->  exit 1
#       FAIL  digest c6a207fc7279 has NO row -- UNRECORDED provenance
#       FAIL  digest 635e3ee7cacd has NO row -- UNRECORDED provenance
#       (4 FAILs total, one per required wiki fix)
#
# That is a preflight step in cut.yml. Pushing the tag in that state would have
# gone red at preflight, SKIPPED the cut job, and spent v1.0.34 for nothing --
# the exact way v1.0.27 through v1.0.31 were burnt. This branch adds the two
# ledger rows, so the gate now passes on content that was actually pulled and
# grepped rather than on a row somebody typed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PINS BELOW ARE MEASURED, NOT ASSERTED
#
# The wiki binding, checked against the registry rather than the PR body that
# claimed it:
#
#     ghcr 0.1.18 ostler-wiki-site      sha256:635e3ee7...  == install.sh pin
#     ghcr 0.1.18 ostler-wiki-compiler  sha256:c6a207fc...  == install.sh pin
#     CM044 v0.1.18 tag  ->  bf5dfe68ad67c0707b802d76cb7658736e8c4282
#     the nav fix bf5dfe68 IS in v0.1.18 and is NOT in v0.1.17 (both measured)
#
# The daemon, checked against the published sidecar rather than the Makefile
# comment that names it:
#
#     gui/Makefile   DAEMON_VERSION 0.4.58  DAEMON_SHA256 d4f274cb...
#     install.sh     OSTLER_ASSISTANT_VERSION 0.4.58
#     install.sh     DEFAULT_ASSISTANT_TARBALL_SHA256 d4f274cb...
#     published      hub-v0.4.58 .tar.gz.sha256          d4f274cb...   ALL FOUR AGREE
#
# CM051 names main at the time of writing. This branch does NOT touch
# install.sh (measured: 0 install.sh paths in its diff), so the pin and the
# shipping tree agree by CONTENT and not merely by ordering:
#
#     CM051 pin 25cc231d  install.sh blob  fb49d304d893249f3c7fc3b124cfe51b5a78d1e8
#     origin/main         install.sh blob  fb49d304d893249f3c7fc3b124cfe51b5a78d1e8
#
# RE-VERIFY IMMEDIATELY BEFORE PUSHING THE TAG, AFTER THE LAST MERGE, NOT
# BEFORE IT:
#
#     git rev-parse $CM051:install.sh
#     git rev-parse origin/main:install.sh
#
# If they diverge, re-point CM051 to main and re-run. A pin chosen early and
# trusted is the thing that burnt v1.0.31.
# ============================================================================

# The daemon. hub-v0.4.58, signed, notarised and stapled. Unchanged from
# v1.0.33 -- v1.0.34 rebuilds no daemon, because every fix in the 33-commit
# delta is install-side or vendored-parser-side and needs no re-sign. This is
# the DEREFERENCED commit: the tag is ANNOTATED and its tag object is
# 87cd9d9e, and recording that would pin the cut to a tag object rather than
# to source.
DAEMON_COMMIT=5b7efb00a541

# The CM051 tree whose install.sh ships in the DMG. See the blob note above.
CM051=25cc231d4dfd8ed9c3a40d0aa2a1df6f3d258061
